notes: Most of us know the left side. A figure is updated for one talk, copied into another, cropped for a third, and after a few months nobody is sure which file has the current version. HUANDENG keeps the slides in one project, called Main Slides. A Presentation, such as a group-meeting talk or a conference talk, is a list of references to those slides, with its own order and its own speaker notes. Edit the Fig. 2 slide once, and every talk that references it shows the new version. If one talk must stay exactly as it was, for example a submitted defence, you pin a named version of that slide in that talk. This is a concept diagram, not a screenshot; the file names are illustrations.
